## Fresh-engine rebuild sequence

1. Try official `engine-backup --mode=restore --scope=all` first if a backup exists.
2. If there is no backup, deploy a fresh OLVM 4.5 Engine with the same FQDN where possible.
3. Create the data center and cluster(s) that match the old compatibility level and CPU family.
4. Recreate logical networks from this report, then add VLAN/bond/bridge details from the per-host command output.
5. Add hosts one at a time. Use maintenance windows; a host may need VDSM certificate/bootstrap cleanup before it accepts the new Engine.
6. Attach/import existing storage domains through the Administration Portal or Engine API. Do not initialize or wipe old storage domains.
7. Import/register VMs and templates from the recovered storage domains. Validate disks, NIC profiles, MAC addresses, boot order, and HA settings.
8. Recreate users, permissions, quotas, affinity groups, scheduling policies, fencing/PM settings, MAC pools, and external providers manually from other records.

